# A long kernel operation through the capability core's `Kernel` hooks is
# preempted and restarted from the idle path, as M5's restarted system calls
# will be (docs/design.md, "Reset and preemption"). The kernel clears up to
# 16 MiB of a free USABLE range from the top down in 4 KiB chunks, like an
# untyped reset, with a preemption point after each chunk that polls the
# local APIC's IRR. It must be preempted by the timer and by an injected
# preemption, in whichever order they come, restart from the idle path each
# time, and leave the range zero; the kernel checks all of this before it
# passes. It reports the longest stretch between two polls (Open questions:
# "Is 4 KiB the right chunk?").
cmdline: test=preempt
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=preempt"
expect: cpu: physical address width
expect: preempt: clearing
expect: preempt: pass 1: range filled with 0xa5
expect: preempt: restart 1 from the idle path
expect: the range is zero
expect: restarts from the idle path after
expect: polls; the longest stretch between two took
expect: TEST PASS
